      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sprang up in the late 1800s when the Valley Railroad crossed Jones’s land, turning a modest farm into a rail‑connected market hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Escalon%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Escalon’s founder, Johnny Jones, planted the first grain in the area in 1852, later expanding to 8,000 acres and pioneering local agriculture.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Escalon%2C_California",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The city’s early growth relied on six‑to‑twelve‑horse teams that plowed fields, a testament to the hard‑working pioneers who built Escalon’s rural roots.",
